# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for tonight's four-card window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/serve-3 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN.
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. Every value is final.
# ORDER.txt says the order, each job's image, its stop rule and its minutes. The image is tp4-serve-3 throughout: T1 builds it, the
# later jobs serve it, and a commit after T1's tag needs a new tag and every later job the new one.
# T3: G1 on the same image and the same smoke: general-tp4 (native vLLM, no speculative decoding). Its numbers sit beside T1's and
# T2's on the same clock under the same night's host load; S2 and G1 are compared on coding text as well, so the two
# coding-text concurrency tests run here too. Sanity check against the recorded G1 runs (within 10%): concurrent4 mean 21.27 and
# 21.10, coding 23.4-24.0; concurrent4_steady is G1's first measurement.
# Duration (estimate): 15 min. Skip it if the window runs short and compare against the recorded G1 numbers for coding,
# long_real_text and concurrent4 only.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-3
C2_PROFILE=general-tp4
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,long_real_text,concurrent4,concurrent4_steady,concurrent4_code,concurrent4_code_equal
